0030-suspend-graphics-in-background.patch -- tell the host when the app leaves the foreground. docs/ENGINE-UPDATE.md section 6; docs/UPSTREAM-AUDIT.md section 4 (Grizzy's 84 lines of
kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorBackgroundExecutionNotPermitted) and section 5 item 3.
Applied by scripts/build-app.sh to its copy of the C# snapshot (patch -p1, run in the project folder) in file-name order, after 0010 and 0020 (and after 0030-import-and-download-never-delete-first); app/gameapp/ is not edited.
Touches GameAppExternal.cs and GameAppMain.cs only, away from every hunk of 0010, 0020, 0030-import, 0031 and 0032.
  * GameAppExternal.cs, GameAppHost: Background(entering) and Active(entering), calling the host's own lifecycle entries through ibuilder_host_symbol (the dlsym the gamepad entries use), in the order
    the engine's front end takes (dm/ios/Sources/front_ios.m front_ios_focus_event 0..3): DidEnterBackground -> dm_focus_set(3), dm_audio_suspend(1), guest_clock_freeze_for(1, 1), dm_gfx_suspend(1);
    WillEnterForeground -> dm_gfx_suspend(0), guest_clock_freeze_for(1, 0), dm_audio_suspend(0), dm_focus_set(2); WillResignActive / DidBecomeActive -> dm_focus_set(2) / (1).
    Every entry is looked up at the call: a host not loaded yet (no game booted) or without one makes the call a no-op. The host exports dm_gfx_suspend(int) for both directions (there is no dm_gfx_resume).
  * GameAppMain.cs, GameAppGameViewController.ViewDidLoad: the four UIApplication notifications, registered with the view's other observers (removed with them in ViewDidDisappear), so they exist only while a game's window does.
  Not done here (the engine's event 0 also does it, front_ios.m): dm_gamepad_reset / dm_movie_active on resign-active, and the audio session re-activation on return (front_ios_audio_session is a stub in
  load/glue_front_standin.m). NOT COMPILED, NOT RUN ON A DEVICE: C# cannot be built here; the function-pointer calls follow GameAppMain.RegisterShaderTranslator's `delegate* unmanaged` use.
